            {
              "id": "1770569419543_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Your entire knowledge is limited ONLY to information contained in this prompt. Do not include any information for demo or sample purposes that is not referenced in the variables below. Only include one output, do not suggest any alternatives.\n## Context\nestimate number: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.estimateNumber}} \nestimate title: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.estimateTitle}}\ndocument type: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.documentType}}\ndocument number: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.documentNumber}}\npurchase order: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.purchaseOrder}}\nitem description: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.itemDescription}}\nasset number: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.assetNumber}}\nestimate expiration date: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.expirationDate}}\ntotal estimate amount: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.totalEstimate}}\ndiscount amount: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input. discountAmount}}\n## Instructions\nAssume the role of a service agent communicating the service estimate details to a customer contact. Your task is to write a professional and courteous email sharing the estimate details and seeking the customer's confirmation to proceed with the work.\n- Make sure to use the estimate number in the generated email subject.\n- When generating email messages, do not include the term \"subject\" in the subject line. Simply provide the subject line content without prefacing it with the word \"subject\".\n - Using the estimate title, document type, document number, purchase order, item description, total estimate amount and discount amount generate Estimate Summary email.\n-  Ensure to quote the purchase order number only if it's value is given, as a source for the estimate.\n-  Mention the document type and document number if given, as a reference for the estimate.\n- Do not repeat the estimate number and estimate title in the email body.\n- Do not use currency symbols in the email body.\n- Use the asset number and item description together if asset number is also provided.\n -Avoid Using verbose suggesting commitments or promises unless explicitly stated in Estimate Title.\n- Mention that the total estimate amount is the net estimated charge for the service.\n- Mention that total estimate amount has been arrived after applying the applicable discounts, only if the discount amount is provided.\n  -Incorporate the essence of Estimate Title, item description and total estimate amount into the generated email body without directly including it in its original form.\n- Do not list out the input information in the email body, rather use the information descriptively.\n - Utilize the Estimate expiration date specified to ask for a response within that date. However, refrain from directly reproducing it in any form, and avoid making direct references to actions within the generated text.\n- Mention that the estimate document is added as an attachment with the email.\n- Mention that further details of the estimates can be referred from the attached document.\n- Make no assumptions and only Include information directly provided.\n- Do not discuss or allude to any unknown or empty variables in the context.\n- Do not  discuss details that are not explicitly included in the context.\n- Format and compose email body in a formal tone for professionalism.\n - Create opening comments with \"Hello,\".\n - Create a closing comment with \"Best regards,\".\n- Ensure that all responses strictly adhere to the provided inputs and context. do not generate or infer any information that is not explicitly supplied in the context. Stick closely to the facts and details given.\n- Do not use bold section headings.\n- Please generate the output text without using any markup indicators such as asterisks for bold or other formatting symbols. provide plain text only.\n- Format the message as an HTML snippet.\n- Begin and end your message with <p>.\n- Do not use the new line character \"\\n\". Instead, use line break tags, \"<br>\".\n- The message should not contain a subject or header with h2 or h3 tags.\n## Output Format\nYour entire response/output is going to consist of a single JSON object {}, and do NOT wrap it within JSON md markers.\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format:\n    {\n        \"emailSubject\": \"<insert generated comments>\",\n        \"emailBody\": \"<insert generated comments>\"\n    }"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"emailBody\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"emailSubject\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
